im][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]snippet_target_mode.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/snippet_target_mode.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-j3[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-j3/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Snippet destination resolution, the new config field, and the [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]collision index[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]target[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]target: add the `ace.snippet_config_path` config field with its schema [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and default, lift snippet-location discovery out of the modals package [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into a UI-free module, add the chezmoi-aware destination resolver and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the pure trigger-collision index, and make the existing unified save [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel honor the configured destination.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Snippet panes in the prompt stack model[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]model: teach PromptStackState about at most one pinned bottom snippet [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane that never participates in launch, stash, or save-as payloads, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the agent-pane accessors and structural invariants, and convert every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane-count call site through an audited table pinned by tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Trigger-name panel with live collision evidence[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]name[dim] · [dim][/dim]after target[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]name: build the trigger-name panel that validates as you type, shows [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]where a colliding trigger already lives and what saving would shadow, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lets the destination be overridden for the session, and returns the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing definition body when the user commits to an existing trigger.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The gt keymap, pane lifecycle, and exact cursor restoration[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pane[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model, name[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane: add the `gt` / `Ctrl+G t` keymap and its hint, open the named [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snippet pane at the bottom of the stack, keep cursor and vim mode per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane so closing the snippet pane returns to the exact prior position, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and enforce the discard-confirmation and last-agent-pane guard rails.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Save confirmation with a real diff, the write, and follow-up [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]actions[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]save[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pane[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]save: route `<enter>` in the snippet pane to a confirmation panel with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]draft/existing/diff views and an external-change guard, reuse the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing snippet write, session publish, and post-write action chain, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and close the pane only after the write succeeds.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Visual language for the snippet pane[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]visual[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pane[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual: give the snippet pane its own theme-safe look — a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trigger-labeled separator rule, a distinct pane accent, new/overwrite [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and dirty states, and its own subtitle — and pin it with PNG snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Help modal and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after name, save, visual[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: add the new keymap to the `?` help popup's Prompt Input section [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and document the snippet authoring loop and the new config field in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`docs/ace.md` and `docs/configuration.md`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end verification of the snippet loop[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: run the full verification gate and drive the real TUI through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]creating, editing, shadow-warning, discarding, and chezmoi-backed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snippet saves, confirming the cursor returns exactly and no launch path [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regressed.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-j3","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-j3.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-96959952b663d8a4c8d3eda9cf08b2f4","started_at":"2026-08-10T18:54:01.600474+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_